      "content": "It is completely valid to acknowledge that highways currently provide essential, high-speed freight logistics and familiar mobility for many residents. A robust economic plan must recognize these immediate burdens of daily commerce and adjust funding to subsidize intermodal hubs that connect rail to rural areas rather than relying solely on new highway mileage. Fairly weighing these needs requires transparent data to show where transit actually drives local jobs alongside the freight companies that depend on existing roads, ensuring the goal is complementary growth rather than replacement.",
